theme_override_colors/font_color = Color(0.85, 0.9, 0.95, 1)
theme_override_font_sizes/font_size = 10
text = "MARS DEEP: DESIGN. LAUNCH. EXPLORE.
NASA Space Apps Challenge 2026 Submission

1. EDUCATIONAL CHALLENGE & VISION
MARS DEEP makes real-world aerospace engineering and astrobiological exploration understandable and exciting for students and players of all ages. By connecting genuine mathematical formulas (Tsiolkovsky rocket equation, antenna link budgets, solar irradiance decay, and hyperbolic atmospheric entry energy) directly to playable 3D flight mechanics, players learn through direct agency.

2. NASA TECHNOLOGIES & INSTRUMENTS REPRESENTED
• Perseverance (Mars 2020) & Curiosity Rovers (Rocker-Bogie 6-Wheel Kinematics)
• SuperCam Laser-Induced Breakdown Spectrometer (LIBS & Raman Optics)
• PIXL Planetary Instrument for X-ray Lithochemistry
• SHERLOC Deep UV Raman & Luminescence Spectrometer
• MOXIE Mars Oxygen In-Situ Resource Utilization Experiment (5.8 g/h O2)
• RIMFAX Radar Imager for Mars' Subsurface Experiment (GPR 10m depth)
• MEDA Mars Environmental Dynamics Analyzer (Meteorology & Dust)
• Atlas V 541, Falcon Heavy & Space Launch System (SLS Block 1B)
• UltraFlex Circular Solar Arrays & MMRTG Radioisotope Power

3. OFFICIAL NASA/JPL DATASETS UTILIZED
• NASA Planetary Fact Sheets: Mars gravitational acceleration (3.721 m/s²), atmospheric boundary conditions, and orbital eccentricity.
• NASA JPL Horizons Ephemerides: Earth-Mars Hohmann transfer geometries (180d & 260d).
• NASA PDS (Planetary Data System): Jezero Crater delta mineralogy and smectite clay compositions.

4. SCIENTIFIC & LEGAL DISCLAIMER
This educational game simulation was created independently for the NASA Space Apps Challenge hackathon. While based rigorously on open NASA and JPL scientific datasets, MARS DEEP is an educational simulation game and does not represent an official endorsement or direct software product of the National Aeronautics and Space Administration."
autowrap_mode = 3

